          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The concept of smooth
            = succeed "-stack" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+%E2%88%9E-groupoid"}> smooth ∞-groupoid
                \.
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifold"}> ∞-orbifold
                \.
          %p Following the logic described at
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivation+for+sheaves%2C+cohomology+and+higher+stacks"} motivation for sheaves, cohomology and higher stacks
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
          %p
            a
            %em
              smooth
              = succeed "-stack" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-categorification"} ∞-categorification
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+space"} smooth space
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stack"} differentiable stack
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stack"} ∞-stack
            on the (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+small+category"}> essentially small
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            of smooth
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ball
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Diff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ball \subset Diff
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CartSp"} CartSp
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Diff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \subset Diff
            (see
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+space"} smooth space
            for more on that).
          %p
            So smooth
            = succeed "-stacks" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            that computes
            %em smooth
            generalized
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology"} cohomology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+Nonabelian+Cohomology"} differential nonabelian cohomology
            and the disucssion under “Models” below for more on that).
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CartSp
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi m
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi Diff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp = \{ (\mathbb{R}^n \to \mathbb{R}^m) \in Diff| n,m \in \mathbb{N}\} \subset Diff
            be the full subcategory [of  on the  of the simple form , equipped with the standard structure of a  with the  given by  of manifolds.]
          %p Then
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Smooth
                  %mn ∞
                  %mi Grpd
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi CartSp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Smooth\infty Grpd := (\infty,1)Sh(CartSp)
          %p
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} (∞,1)-topos
            given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+of+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-sheaves"} (∞,1)-category of (∞,1)-sheaves
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp
          %p
            This is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
          %h2#models Models
          %p
            There is a large number of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model structures
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} presenting
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi H
                      %mi Diff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}_{Diff}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} model structures on simplicial (pre)sheaves
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp
          %h3#in_terms_of_groupoids_internal_to_smooth_spaces
            In terms of
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            Notice for instance that there is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sheaves"} model structure on simplicial sheaves
            given by the category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi CartSp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SSh(CartSp)
            equipped with the injective
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves"} local model structure on simplicial presheaves
          %p But sheaves on cartesian spaces
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi CartSp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo :
                  %mi SmoothSp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Sh(CartSp)
                  \=: SmoothSp
          %p
            is the category of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+spaces"} smooth spaces
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi CartSp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SSh(CartSp)
            is just the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects"} simplicial objects
            of that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi CartSp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %msup
                    %mi SmoothSp
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  SSh(CartSp)
                  \\simeq
                  SmoothSp^{\Delta^{op}}
                  \\,.
          %p
            So one model for smooth
            = succeed "-stacks" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object"} simplicial
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+spaces"} smooth spaces
          %p
            Notice that the fibrant object in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi SmoothSp
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmoothSp^{\Delta^{op}}
            are the globally
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi SmoothSp
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mi op
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi CartSp
                  %mo ,
                  %mi SSet
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  SmoothSp^{\Delta^{op}}
                  \\simeq
                  Sh(CartSp, SSet)
                  \\,,
          %p
            that satisfy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent+for+simplicial+presheaves"} descent for simplicial presheaves
          %p
            Being
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CartSp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp
            with values in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
          %p
            Moreover, the
            = succeed "-condition" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CartSp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp
            is comparatively trivial, and in many cases (…details eventually here, but see examples below…) entirely empty, as every cartesian space is (smoothly, even) contractible.
          %p
            This means that the fibrant objects in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SSh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi CartSp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SSh(CartSp)
            are pretty much nothing but
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+spaces"} smooth spaces
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            = succeed "-groupoid" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            In particular
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
            internal to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
            are therefore a model for smooth
            = succeed "-stacks." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            Moreover, a morphism between smooth
            = succeed "-stacks" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctor"} anafunctor
            (see
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+localization"} simplicial localization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+category"} homotopy category
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
            for details).
          %p
            The model of smooth
            = succeed "-stacks" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-groupoids" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctors"} anafunctors
            as morphism between them is the model used in the
            = succeed "-ian" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Baez"} Baez
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+infinity-bundle"} higher principal bundles
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/Differential+Nonabelian+Cohomology"} differential nonabelian cohomology
          %h3#examples Examples
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi SmoothSp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  Diff \hookrightarrow SmoothSp
          %p
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            into
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+spaces"} smooth spaces
            we may regard
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            naturally as a sheaf on CartSp.
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B} G
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+space"} SmoothSp
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo :
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N :
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grpd"} Grpd
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo →
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SSet"} SSet
            this yields a
            = succeed "-valued" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \mathbf{B} G
            which we shall by convenient and useful abuse of notation just call
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B} G
            itself.
          %p
            Notice that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B} G
            does not satisfy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            when regarded as a simplicial sheaf on all of
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-stackification"} ∞-stackification
            is instead
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mi Bund
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G Bund(-)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stack"} stack
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundles"} principal bundles
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mi Bund
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi U
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi groupoid
                  %mi of
                  %mi G
                  %mo −
                  %mi bundles
                  %mi on
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G Bund(-) : U \mapsto groupoid of G-bundles on U
          %p
            (or rather, in our context of simplicial sheaves, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rectified+infinity-stack"} rectification
            of that).
          %p
            But restricted to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi CartSp
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CartSp
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+presheaf"} simplicial sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B} G
            %em does
            satisfy
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent"} descent
            = succeed "-bundle" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mi Bund
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≃
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Diff
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mi n
                  %mo ,
                  %mi G
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G Bund(\mathbb{R}^n) \simeq (\mathbf{B} G)(\mathbb{R}^n)
                  \:= \mathbf{B}(Diff(\mathbb{R}^n,  G))
          %p
            for each
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            is a fibrant object in the injective
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sheaves"} model structure on simplicial sheaves
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+fibrant+objects"} category of fibrant objects
            apply to
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+universal+bundle"} universal G-bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi E
                  %mi G
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{E} G \to \mathbf{B}G
            regarded as a smooth
            = succeed "-stack" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi E
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo *
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi d
                                %mn 0
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi d
                                %mn 1
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbf{E}G &amp;\to&amp; {*}
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\mathbf{B}G &amp;\stackrel{d_0}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B}G
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow^{d_1}
                  \\\
                  \\mathbf{B}G
                  }
          %p
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi SmoothSp
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi Δ
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SmoothSp^{\Delta^{op}}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
            being
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+adjoint"} right adjoint
            is the same as the image under the nerve of the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            in sheaves of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoids"} groupoids
            (so that still our notational suppressing of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            is justified).
          %p etc.
